Buggy App RCA
* Capture Logs
    Logs are written to app.log when the Flask app runs.

* Reproduce Issue
    Run the app locally and send multiple requests to the / endpoint:
        "for i in {1..10}; do curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://localhost:5055/; done"
    You’ll observe intermittent HTTP 500 errors caused by random failures.
        Example output:
        200
        500
        200
        500
        200
* Root Cause
    The random failures occur because of this line in the code:
        if random.choice([True, False]):
            raise Exception("Simulated random failure!")
    This intentionally raises an unhandled exception, causing Flask to return a 500 Internal Server Error.
    There’s no error-handling logic to catch and manage this exception gracefully.
    ![alt text](image.png)
* Proposed Fix
    Add proper exception handling to prevent the app from crashing.
    Fixed Code (Conceptual)
        @app.route('/')
        def home():
            app.logger.info("Home endpoint hit")
            try:
                if random.choice([True, False]):
                    raise Exception("Simulated random failure!")
                return jsonify({"message": "App is working fine"})
            except Exception as e:
                app.logger.error(f"Error occurred: {e}")
                return jsonify({"error": str(e)}), 500